{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>From his youth.</b> It is written מִנְּעֻרָיו — from the time he is shaken loose to emerge from his mother's womb, the evil impulse is placed in him." "<b>לא אסף ולא אסף.</b> He doubled the statement for an oath; as it is written ״אֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּעְתִּי מֵעֲבֹר מֵי נֹחַ״ (Isaiah 54:9) — and we do not find in it an oath, except this doubling of His words, and that is the oath. And so the Sages expounded in tractate Shevuot."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:03.421464191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}